      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test file and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. The key understandability issues are:\n1. Dead code: `data_valid()` and `data_invalid()` are defined but never used by any test\n2. Multiple bare assertions in one method with no differentiation between cases\n3. Unused imports from the dead data methods\n\nI'll refactor the test to use a parameterized test with a named argument stream for clarity.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test removes dead code (`data_valid`/`data_invalid` and unused imports) and replaces the flat list of assertions with a `@ParameterizedTest` driven by a named `monthAmounts()` stream, making the input→expected mapping explicit and each case independently identifiable."
    }
